            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# UsageMonitor 0.1.2

- Antigravity: the quota now stays current while Antigravity is closed.
  UsageMonitor starts Antigravity's own language server in the background,
  with no window, and reads the quota from it. It uses the sign-in Antigravity
  already has, and stops when Antigravity opens, when UsageMonitor quits, or
  after 20 minutes without a reading. Antigravity has to be installed and
  signed in once. PRIVACY.md describes what this server sends to Google and
  where it keeps its state.
]]></description>
